==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|recommendacioun}}, from {{der|en|xno|recomendacion}}, from {{der|en|ML.|recommendatio}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌɹɛkəmɛnˈdeɪʃən/|/ˌɹɛkəmənˈdeɪʃən/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-recommendation.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪʃən|s=5}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# An act of [[recommend]]ing.
# That which is recommended.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Aisha Salaudeen|title=Nigeria reopens churches, mosques and hotels amid rising cases of Covid-19|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2020/06/02/africa/religious-gatherings-nigeria/index.html|date=2020-06-02|passage=Some of the '''recommendations''' made by the PTF to prevent the spread of Covid-19 as religious institutions and hotels open up include: managed access to markets and locations of economic activity to limit the risk of transmitting Covid-19, mandatory use of face masks and temperature checks in public places, and information campaigns on the dangers of the virus among others.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Brenda Goodman|title=CDC considers narrowing its Covid-19 vaccine recommendations|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2025/04/16/health/cdc-risk-based-covid-19-vaccine-recommendation/index.html|date=2025-04-16|passage=
The US Centers and Disease Control and Prevention is considering recommending annual Covid-19 shots to those who are older or who have compromised immune function, rather than the current blanket '''recommendation''' for everyone 6 months of age and older.}}
# A [[commendation]] or [[endorsement]].
#: {{ux|en|Your next employer may require a '''recommendation'''.}}
# A [[suggestion]] or [[proposal]] about the best course of action (with [[adposition]]s including "[[about]]" for the context and "[[to]]" for the course of action)
#: ''He made a '''recommendation''' about what food to order.''
#: ''We followed the '''recommendation''' to order sushi''.

